# Mintlify publishes index.mdx plus api-docs/ (see docs.json). Everything else
# in this repo is pipeline / Evidence.dev markdown whose template syntax is not
# MDX and must not be parsed by the Mintlify GitHub Deployment check.
# Keep every entry below ignored: dashboard/ and webapp/ in particular contain
# Evidence template syntax that the MDX parser cannot read. New documentation
# pages go in api-docs/, never in docs/.
dashboard/
webapp/
src/
tests/
docs/
scripts/
migrations/
.claude/
.agents/
.github/
.codex/
cache/
temp/
# Local virtualenv: vendored package READMEs are not MDX and break
# `mint broken-links` before it reaches api-docs/. Gitignored, so CI never
# saw it; this makes the local run usable too.
.venv/

# Root-level *.md, decided explicitly.
#
# The entries above are all directories, so until now every Markdown file at
# the repository root sat inside Mintlify's parse scope while being absent from
# docs.json's navigation — published in the sense that the URL resolves, but
# invisible in the sidebar, and neither state chosen on purpose.
#
# The decision: `skill.md` IS published, deliberately. It is the agent loader,
# api-docs/agents.mdx and llms.txt both link to it by URL, and an agent that
# fetches https://octo-98895abd.mintlify.site/skill.md must get the file rather
# than a 404. It stays out of the sidebar because a human has no use for it.
# So it is NOT listed here.
#
# The other three are repository documentation for people working ON SILO, not
# on the API, and they are ignored so that neither `mint broken-links` nor the
# published site treats them as pages:
README.md
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
